From 9cdd9d0dc1afa6ee0baf1ef7273a5ed46cd00da5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: auditor <audit@local>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 22:24:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 01/10] Dockerfile: COPY the full import closure of main.py;
 test enforces it

INVARIANT PROTECTED: a deployed image must be able to reach `startup()`.

Finding (audit S9): `python3 main.py` inside the image as shipped raised
ModuleNotFoundError for market_data (bybit_connection.py:73), memory
(main.py:49), project_status (main.py:51) and session_log (main.py:52).
The container therefore died before the health server bound, the
HEALTHCHECK never went green and any orchestrator restart-looped it.
Deployability of the tree as uploaded was zero.

Why this is the first patch: every other property of the shell - the
single-writer ledger, reconcile-before-trade, the kill switch - is worth
nothing in a process that cannot import itself.

What changed:
  Dockerfile      - COPY list = static import closure of main.py
                    (incl. the lazy ml_strategy/policy/features imports
                    behind POLICY_MODE, and signals/ for shadow.py)
  tests/test_dockerfile.py - recomputes the closure with `ast` and fails
                    if the Dockerfile omits any of it; also refuses a
                    `COPY . /app` regression (that is how the predecessor
                    baked live keys into layers).

What did NOT change: .dockerignore still excludes .env, state/, data/,
tests/, tools/. artifacts/ is still not shipped; on this tree that means
promotion_gate refuses inside the image, which is the correct default.

Verification: new test fails on baseline (missing 8 files), passes after.
